## 2. Full sync through the anti-corruption layer
   concept: the client pages with @odata.nextLink and retries 429/503, honouring Retry-After; the translator maps CRM fields and option-set codes to domain types; the domain's invariants reject what is wrong; rejects go to quarantine
   employers: 3 applied
   [retry] 429 on GET Contacts (next page), Retry-After: 1 -> wait 1000 ms, attempt 2
   members: fetched 120 in 3 pages, applied 116, rejected 4; mark null -> 2026-09-04T10:10:00Z
   quarantined M0017 c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000011: email 'jamie.dupont.at.example.org' is not an address
   quarantined (no number) c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000021: New_MemberNo is empty
   quarantined M0058 c0000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000003a: New_SchemeStatus 100000003 is not a known scheme status
   quarantined M0091 c0000000-0000-4000-8000-00000000005b: birth date '2031-02-01' is not a past date
   check ok: a 429 was retried after waiting at least its Retry-After (1 s)
   check ok: 120 contacts fetched over 3 pages: 116 members applied, 4 quarantined
   check ok: the unknown option-set code 100000003 is quarantined, not mapped to a guess
   check ok: $select kept unread CRM fields out: no notes or phone in what crossed the boundary
   check ok: members in Postgres: 116, and every one passes the domain's constraints

## 3. Incremental sync with a high-water mark
   concept: ask only for ModifiedOn ge <mark>, in ModifiedOn order, move the mark after the run; ge, not gt, because the mark has second precision
   CRM users edited M0003, M0004, M0005 (webhooks off for this step: the scheduled sync alone)
   GET Contacts?$filter=ModifiedOn ge 2026-09-04T10:10:00Z&$orderby=ModifiedOn asc,ContactId asc
   fetched 4, applied 3, unchanged 1 (the row at the mark itself comes back; its version makes it a no-op); mark -> 2026-10-03T15:00:48Z
   check ok: the incremental sync applied exactly the 3 edits
   check ok: M0004's option-set code 100000002 arrived as the domain status 'retired'
   [retry] 503 on GET Contacts, Retry-After: none -> wait 15 ms, attempt 2
   M0006 and M0007 were edited in the same second 2026-10-03T15:00:48Z, with a sync in between
   ModifiedOn gt 2026-10-03T15:00:48Z: 0 rows (M0007 would be lost for good); ModifiedOn ge 2026-10-03T15:00:48Z: 5 rows
   next sync (ge): fetched 5, applied 1, unchanged 4
   check ok: gt would miss the second write of the same second; ge picks it up and the repeat is a no-op

## 4. Webhooks: signed, fresh, once
   concept: HMAC-SHA256 over '<timestamp>.<body>', constant-time compare, a 300 s window, the event id from the signed body as idempotency key; the event is a hint: the app re-reads the record
   CRM delivered event 56a30a84: x-crm-timestamp 1791039648, x-crm-signature v1=4044130dc5dd0d5ef...
   app answered 200 {"status":"processed","outcome":"applied"}
   check ok: a genuine delivery is verified and applied
   duplicate delivery (the CRM retried, new timestamp, same event): 200 {"status":"duplicate","deliveries":2,"outcome":"applied"}; inbox: deliveries=2, outcome=applied
   check ok: a duplicate delivery is acknowledged and not processed again
   forged: body changed, original signature -> 401 {"error":"signature does not match"}
   forged: signed with a guessed secret -> 401 {"error":"signature does not match"}
   check ok: forged deliveries are refused with 401
   replay of the captured delivery 6 minutes later (exact bytes, valid signature) -> 401 {"error":"timestamp outside the 300s window (age 361s)"}
   the same replay inside the window -> 200 {"status":"duplicate","deliveries":3,"outcome":"applied"}
   check ok: an old delivery is refused by the window; inside the window the event id catches it
   check ok: 3 refusals logged, and the forged event changed nothing

## 5. Writing back with ETags
   concept: PATCH with If-Match on the version last seen; 412 means someone changed the record since: re-read, re-apply if they did not touch our field, otherwise report a conflict
   [retry] 429 on PATCH Contacts(c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014), Retry-After: 1 -> wait 1000 ms, attempt 2
   PATCH without If-Match -> 428
   [retry] 503 on PATCH Contacts(c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014), Retry-After: none -> wait 190 ms, attempt 2
   M0020: a CRM user changed the phone; the member changes the email -> 200 {"outcome":"updated","version":1131,"attempts":2,"conflicts":1}; CRM now has robin.new@example.org
   check ok: a stale If-Match got 412, the adapter re-read and applied on the new ETag
   [retry] 429 on GET Contacts(c0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015), Retry-After: 1 -> wait 1000 ms, attempt 2
   M0021: a CRM user changed the email too -> 409 {"outcome":"conflict","theirs":"set.by.crm@example.org","attempts":1}; CRM keeps set.by.crm@example.org
   check ok: a real conflict is reported (409), not overwritten

## 6. Nightly reconciliation
   concept: sync sees only what ModifiedOn shows; once a night, compare counts and checksums of the canonical records on both sides, by employer and then by member, and report the drift
   drift made: M0030 hard-deleted in the CRM (no webhook), M0040 renamed by a CRM import that kept an old ModifiedOn, M0050's email edited by hand in the local database
